abstract:
We provide here all the procedures in 	exttt{Mathematica} which are needed for the computation of the analytic images of the strong coupling constant powers in Minkowski (${ ar{\mathfrak A}_{
u}(s;n_f)}$ and ${\mathfrak A_{
u}^	ext{glob}(s)}$) and Euclidean (${ ar{\mathcal A}_{
u}(Q^2;n_f)}$ and ${\mathcal A_{
u}^	ext{glob}(Q^2)}$) domains at arbitrary energy scales (${s}$ and ${Q^2}$, correspondingly) for both schemes --- with fixed number of active flavours ${n_f=3, 4, 5, 6}$ and the global one with taking into account all heavy-quark thresholds. These singularity-free couplings are inevitable elements of Analytic Perturbation Theory (APT) in QCD and its generalization --- Fractional APT, needed to apply the APT imperative for renormalization-group improved hadronic observables.
